+### Research-derived architecture decisions — dated 2026-11-01
+
+| Pattern already used by established agent systems | Primary reference | Orange Invest decision |
+|---|---|---|
+| Anthropic's workflow-vs-agent distinction, simplest composable path | https://www.anthropic.com/research/building-effective-agents | Use one typed language-understanding adapter around a deterministic booking state machine; no multi-agent architecture for a bounded 8-tool local task. |
+| Anthropic's outcome/trace-based evals, code graders + trials | https://www.anthropic.com/research/demystifying-evals-for-ai-agents | Script simulated users; grade provider DB + approval ledger + traces, not reassuring assistant prose. Freeze scenario IDs and seeds. |
+| AWS Bedrock Agents user confirmation and return-of-control | https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/implement-human-in-the-loop-confirmation-with-amazon-bedrock-agents/ | Application/domain controller stores exact approval and owns mutation calls; model's approval text is not an authorization record. |
+| AWS AgentCore with Step Functions deterministic booking validators | https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/validating-multi-agent-decisions-with-step-functions-and-bedrock-agentcore/ | Verify action constraints after agent proposes, **before** provider write; do NOT add AWS/cloud to local mock assignment. |
+| AWS Well-Architected Agentic AI Lens: scoped memory, security, outcomes and traces | https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/agentic-ai-lens/ | Minimal scoped preference memory, trace, human oversight, hard budgets and replay tests. |
+| LangGraph HITL interrupts can replay side effects | https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/blob/main/src/oss/langgraph/interrupts.mdx | Do not run a mutating tool before persistent approval checkpoint; replays require idempotent persisted operations. |
+| Temporal durable execution and retries | https://github.com/temporalio/documentation/blob/main/docs/evaluate/understanding-temporal.mdx | Recover unknown side-effect outcomes with persistent operation IDs / status reads, not blind retry. No Temporal server needed. |
+| AWS Durable Execution explicit no-exactly-once warning | https://docs.aws.amazon.com/durable-execution/patterns/best-practices/idempotency/ | Database uniqueness and provider idempotency keys, not vague exactly-once claims. |
